OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F306A1787015895
OL,3,CGovernment urged to act to make
OL,4,Cteaching profession more attractive
OL,6,FThe union is pressing the Department
OL,7,Fof Education to introduce effective
OL,8,Fmeasures to retain those teachers who
OL,9,Fhave recently started in the
OL,10,Fprofession in the Irish education
OL,11,Fsystem.
OL,13,FTUI president Anthony Quinn said:
OL,14,F"Teachers want to teach, yet it is
OL,15,Fabundantly clear that they are being
OL,16,Fdistracted from teaching and learning
OL,17,Fby increasing administrative workload.
OL,26,@vD@AOU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G2/5
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,307,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30603
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F306A1787015895
OL,3,CGovernment urged to act to make
OL,4,Cteaching profession more attractive
OL,6,F"In a survey of our members earlier
OL,7,Fthis year, 92% agreed that
OL,8,Fbureaucratic workload/paperwork that
OL,9,Fdistracts from teaching has increased
OL,10,Fsince they commenced their career.
OL,12,F"Separately, 92% agreed that
OL,13,F'initiative overload' is leading to
OL,14,Fburnout among teachers and principal
OL,15,Fteachers.
OL,17,F"Put simply, teachers have to spend
OL,18,Ftoo much time on non-teaching workload
OL,19,Fgenerated by constant new programme,
OL,20,Fpolicy and administrative demands.
OL,26,@nD@AOUtD@AOUyD@AOU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G3/5
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,307,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30604
SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F306A1787015895
OL,3,CGovernment urged to act to make
OL,4,Cteaching profession more attractive
OL,6,F"This culture of excessive paperwork
OL,7,Fhas an obvious negative effect on
OL,8,Fteacher retention and must be urgently
OL,9,Faddressed."
OL,11,FMr Quinn also raised concerns around
OL,12,Freduced pension provision, and said
OL,13,Fteachers returning from overseas
OL,14,Fshould have service recognised.
OL,16,FHe added a call for reinstatement of
OL,17,Fsome allowances.
OL,26,@nD@AOUqD@KO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G4/5
